hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1797","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person who recites the Qur'an and is proficient in it will be with the noble, honorable scribes (angels), and the one who recites the Qur'an with difficulty, struggling to read it, will have a double reward."""
